id: pm-mza19c
title: "zsh and fish completions have no docs block, so no pm docs flag ever completes in those shells"
description: "Found 2026-11-11 while adding --full-history to the files, docs and test completions (pm-gh1700). src/sdk/completion/bash.ts has a docs) case listing --add, --add-glob, --remove, --migrate, --note, --validate-paths and --full-history. src/sdk/completion/zsh.ts and src/sdk/completion/fish.ts have no docs block at all, so in those shells pm docs completes no flag, while pm files, its twin, completes every flag. The completions are hand-written per shell, so nothing checks one shell's flag set against another's or against DOCS_FLAG_CONTRACTS. Duplicate check: completion searches; pm-xhot (closed) planned contract-generated completion flags, and pm-6qi8 and pm-mthy (closed) fixed single drifts."
type: Chore
status: open
priority: 3
